  "limitations": [
    "The self-control effect discussed is only valid for hydronic floor heating systems and not for electrically heated floor systems."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This narrative review by Bjarne W. Olesen provides a comprehensive overview of radiant floor heating systems, covering their historical context, thermal comfort implications, indoor air quality benefits, heating and cooling capacities, and control strategies. Key findings indicate that floor heating systems achieve the same operative temperature at lower air temperatures compared to convective systems, offer uniform vertical temperature profiles, and reduce issues like condensation, mold growth, and dust mites. The paper highlights that individual room controls significantly improve energy efficiency (15-30% savings) and that the self-control effect of hydronic floor heating contributes to stable room temperatures. While effective, the self-control mechanism is specific to hydronic systems and not applicable to electrically heated floors."
}